NAME

UBYTE ulibMoveFile - Moves a file catalogue entry and physical file


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibMoveFile(struct FileCat *File1, long OldSubDir, long NewSection,
                               a0                   d0               d1

                   long NewSubDir)
                          d2


DESCRIPTION

This function moves a file catalogue entry (and the physical file) to a new
section and subdirectory.

The <OldSubDir> and <NewSubDir> are file subdirectory numbers of the source
and destination file subdirectories; <OldSubDir> may be set to -1 which will
cause this function to search the available subdirectories in <File1->Section>
for the physical file.

The source section is assumed to be <File1->Section>, and the destination
section is <NewSection>.

Both the file catalogue entry and the physical file (if present) are moved.

Note that it is virtually impossible for failure error #2 to occur, since the
file catalogue is Semaphore-locked at the beginning of the function, and
unlocked at the end; the delete/add is executed as an atomic operation.


RETURNS

0        - Success
Non-zero - Failure

              1 - Catalogue entry not deleted successfully
              2 - Catalogue entry deleted, but unable to re-add file to new
                  section
              3 - Catalogue entry move successful, but physical file is
                  not present on disk
